        "original_id": "05556340-b474-5e4c-9ed5-2ff2c0b45984",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Javier Frana, Thomaz Koch, Patricia Tarabini, Colin Dowdeswell, Colin Dibley\n- Organizations: ESPN Latin America\n- Places: Argentina, Brazil, Porto Alegre\n- Events: French Open, Wimbledon, U.S. National Championships, Turkey Open\n- Roles: tennis player, tennis commentator\n\nFacts:\n- Thomaz Koch was born on May 11, 1945, in Porto Alegre, Brazil.\n- Javier Frana was born on December 25, 1966.\n- Thomaz Koch is a left-handed former tennis player from Brazil.\n- Javier Frana is a former tennis player from Argentina and a current tennis commentator for ESPN Latin America.\n- Thomaz Koch was a quarter-finalist at the French Open, Wimbledon, and the U.S. National Championships.\n- Patricia Tarabini and Javier Frana won the mixed doubles title at the 1996 French Open.\n- At the Turkey Open, Colin Dowdeswell won the singles title.\n- At the Turkey Open, Colin Dibley and Thomaz Koch won the doubles title as partners.",
